ng{\"name\": name, \"email\": email})\n}\n\nNeed refactor. External behavior identical: status codes, response bodies. Note original success response: Content-Type set after possible errors? For errors no Content-Type set. Body exactly {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no newline. 404 body {\"error\":\"not found\"}. 500 body {\"error\":\"db\"}. Success: Content-Type application/json, body JSON encoded map: {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}? Go map encoding sorts keys alphabetically: email then name. json.Encoder adds trailing newline. Need preserve. If we use helper writeJSON maybe for success only? If helper sets Content-Type and encodes, for success same. For errors, if helper sets Content-Type, external behavior changes (headers). User says same status codes, same response bodies, not necessarily headers? But keep external behavior identical likely includes headers? They specifically same status codes, same response bodies. But safer preserve headers: errors no Content-Type. Success Content-Type application/json. Could have writeError(w,", "top2": [[[1596, -0.002889512339606881], [22916, -6.951129913330078]], [[1144, -2.2411597456084564e-05], [14235, -11.839827537536621]], [[4087, -0.009201711975038052], [310, -5.072536945343018]], [[1156, -0.019915714859962463], [303, -4.4288530349731445]], [[579, -0.3031642735004425], [25, -2.137423276901245]], [[1622, -0.0035342369228601456], [3296, -6.687345504760742]], [[13, -0.38003525137901306], [25, -1.3732279539108276]], [[14235, -0.036745183169841766], [1165, -4.069292068481445]], [[89109, -0.257582426071167], [7936, -2.065747022628784]], [[5805, -0.00016249546024482697], [2400, -9.08869743347168]], [[9830, -0.025354953482747078], [6795, -3.7390522956848145]], [[6795, -3.194859891664237e-05], [2952, -11.808908462524414]], [[47781, -1.3027675151824951], [8387, -1.771031141281128]], [[4475, -0.8724247217178345], [2833, -1.184211254119873]], [[2528, -4.696956239058636e-05], [11, -10.005766868591309]], [[11, -0.0008561699069105089]